const e={readingNotes:[{title:{zh:"研究问题",en:"Research question"},body:{zh:"研究讨论预期股票收益与波动之间的关系，并强调该关系取决于建模和信息设定。 阅读时先把它理解为一个被界定的问题，而不是可以脱离样本、时间和制度环境的结论。",en:"“Expected Stock Returns and Volatility” frames a bounded research question. Read the stated question together with the named sample, dates, and institutional setting rather than treating it as a conclusion that automatically travels to another market or period."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1093/rfs/12.4.1009",label:{zh:"Review of Financial Studies (1999) · 来源说明",en:"Review of Financial Studies (1999) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"研究设计",en:"Research design"},body:{zh:"公开设计将收益与条件波动联系起来，关注时变风险和回报的统计刻画。 这说明比较对象、观察窗口和对照关系是研究合同的一部分；改变其中任何一项，都可能改变所检验的命题。",en:"For “Expected Stock Returns and Volatility”, the source describes a deliberate comparison, observation window, and control relation. Those choices are part of its research contract: changing one can change the proposition being tested, even when the method label remains the same."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1093/rfs/12.4.1009",label:{zh:"Review of Financial Studies (1999) · 来源说明",en:"Review of Financial Studies (1999) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"数据与时点",en:"Data and timing"},body:{zh:"需明确收益频率、波动度量、条件信息集、估计窗口与是否使用实现值或模型估计值。 数据字段、可得时点和样本筛选需要与原始研究分开记录，不能仅凭同名变量或最终修订数据就视为可比。",en:"For “Expected Stock Returns and Volatility”, keep the fields, their availability timing, and the sample filters separate from the original study. A same-named variable, later-revised database, or matching end-of-period date is not automatically a comparable input."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1093/rfs/12.4.1009",label:{zh:"Review of Financial Studies (1999) · 来源说明",en:"Review of Financial Studies (1999) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"如何理解结果",en:"How to read the result"},body:{zh:"任何观察到的收益—波动关系都需要放在条件模型和样本背景下解释，不能简化为波动越高回报越高。 它支持的是该来源所描述的经验或理论关系；它本身不把相关性、模型拟合或历史表现升级为因果、可执行性或未来保证。",en:"For “Expected Stock Returns and Volatility”, the source supports only the empirical or theoretical relation it describes. It does not turn association, model fit, or historical performance into causality, a directly executable procedure, or a guarantee about subsequent outcomes."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1093/rfs/12.4.1009",label:{zh:"Review of Financial Studies (1999) · 来源说明",en:"Review of Financial Studies (1999) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"复核清单",en:"Replication checks"},body:{zh:"分别复核波动代理、均值与方差方程、分布假设和样本外划分，并报告估计不确定性。 在做后续分析前，应把这些选择写入版本化的研究记录，并保留原始来源链接与访问日期。",en:"Before extending “Expected Stock Returns and Volatility”, record its sample, timing, construction choices, and source edition in a versioned note. Keep the primary-source link and access date so a later reader can distinguish a changed definition from a changed result."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1093/rfs/12.4.1009",label:{zh:"Review of Financial Studies (1999) · 来源说明",en:"Review of Financial Studies (1999) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"适用边界",en:"Scope boundary"},body:{zh:"该条导读引用 Review of Financial Studies (1999)。历史条件关系不保证未来补偿，也不回答杠杆、流动性或交易成本之后的可实现结果。 若需要量化结论、参数、表格或稳健性检验，请回到原文并单独核对版本、附录与样本定义。",en:"This guide cites Review of Financial Studies (1999) for “Expected Stock Returns and Volatility”. Its public description defines the boundary. For numerical conclusions, parameters, tables, or robustness tests, return to the original and separately verify the edition, appendices, and sample definitions."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1093/rfs/12.4.1009",label:{zh:"Review of Financial Studies (1999) · 来源说明",en:"Review of Financial Studies (1999) · source description"}}}],readerLimits:{zh:"本文只整理“Expected Stock Returns and Volatility”所公开说明的研究问题与设计边界，不构成收益预测、交易规则或全文复现。历史条件关系不保证未来补偿，也不回答杠杆、流动性或交易成本之后的可实现结果。",en:"This guide only organizes the publicly described question and design of “Expected Stock Returns and Volatility”. It is not a return forecast, trading rule, or full-text replication. The source's stated scope remains controlling."}};export{e as default};
